  "notes": "Swedish eurodance/hard-dance with self-sung vocals over a bass-forward track, and the entry gives an unusually direct instruction about where the information lives: he is documented as \"passionate about basslines and uses them in his music\", so \"expect a prominent rolling offbeat or 16th saw bass carrying as much melodic information as the lead\". That is the lowest `followRootsProb` of any four-on-the-floor model in this section, 0.55, with two authored cell shapes and the widest passing-tone set in the hands-up block — the bass is a second melody, not a root pump. The key preference is documented verbatim: \"Basshunter likes to create songs in minor scales\", hence minor keys at a 7:2 weighting and four-chord i-VI-III-VII vamps. The kit is the entry's \"hard kick on all four with a short tail, clap on 2&4, offbeat open hats, and snare rolls into the drop\", with the hard-dance influence showing as \"a compressed, clipped kick that eats the low mids\". Loops are 8 bars, and the supersaw lead doubles the topline. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocities, the cell shapes and the roll ramp; the research calls the tempo and drum detail genre-derived.",
